      "title": "1. Intro",
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "In this video, I will introduce a \"cinemagraph\" workflow that allows you to animate a portion of a still image by applying a mask.\n\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "In this video, I will introduce a \"cinemagraph\" workflow that allows you to animate a portion of a still image by applying a mask.\n\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
    {
      "id": 81,
      "type": "Note",
      "pos": [
        102,
        82
      ],
      "size": [
        624.4818115234375,
        242.27957153320312
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 3,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "2. Draw Mask",
      "properties": {
        "text": ""
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "First, draw a mask on the original image from the \"Load Image\" step.\n\nThe mask should be drawn to cover an appropriate portion.\n\nIf drawn too narrowly, the range of movement may be too limited, and if drawn too widely, unintended movements may create a sense of dissonance.\n\nIn my case, I want to make the hair of Supergirl flutter, so I will apply a mask to the hair part of Supergirl. \n\nFor the hair, if the area above the hair is too wide, it may give the impression that the scalp is moving, so I drew the mask as tightly as possible.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "First, draw a mask on the original image from the \"Load Image\" step.\n\nThe mask should be drawn to cover an appropriate portion.\n\nIf drawn too narrowly, the range of movement may be too limited, and if drawn too widely, unintended movements may create a sense of dissonance.\n\nIn my case, I want to make the hair of Supergirl flutter, so I will apply a mask to the hair part of Supergirl. \n\nFor the hair, if the area above the hair is too wide, it may give the impression that the scalp is moving, so I drew the mask as tightly as possible.\n"
      },
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
